paras.en:
When the prince displayed his splendour on the skirt of the saddle,
then the saddle taunted the radiant sun;
the steed in pride did not set its hoof on the ground;
in haste it said: “Spread the carpet on the highest Throne!”
He took the falcon of fate in his grip by the eyelashes;
in the vice of his armpits he imprisoned the wind.

There was a world of amazement, whether the divine or the human realm;
all repented of sin, whether Harut or Marut;
all were yellow with fear, whether the sun or the ruby;
the sultans were stunned, neither throne nor coffin.
When the brilliance of the radiant face put them beside themselves,
the sky propped its hands on the ground above the earth.

From the tracks of the steed the earth came into a whirl;
but the devotee of the Truth became drenched in sweat.
On the face the water of perspiration showed a strange sight;
by those drops a cloud of shame spread over the spring rain.
